## Swagger
http://localhost:8000/docs

## API Overview

### Request/Response Examples
🔹 GET /prices/latest
Description:
Fetches the latest market price for a given symbol from the specified data provider.

Query Parameters:

Name	Type	Required	Description
symbol	string	✅ Yes	The stock/asset symbol
provider	string	❌ No	Data provider (e.g., yfinance, alpha_vantage). Defaults to system default if omitted.

Responses:
Code	Description
200	Success
400	Invalid request parameters
404	Data not found

Example Request:
GET http://localhost:8000/prices/latest?symbol=OP&provider=yfinance
Example Response:
{
  "symbol": "OP",
  "price": 1.61,
  "timestamp": "2025-06-15T10:11:14.544141",
  "provider": "yfinance"
}
🔹 POST /prices/poll
Description:
Starts a polling job that fetches market prices at regular intervals for one or more symbols.

Request Body:
{
  "symbols": ["TSLA", "MSFT"],
  "provider": "yfinance",
  "interval": 20
}
Field	Type	Required	Description
symbols	string[]	✅ Yes	List of asset symbols to poll
provider	string	✅ Yes	Data provider (e.g., yfinance)
interval	int	✅ Yes	Polling interval in seconds

Responses:

Code	Description
201	Job accepted and started
400	Invalid request payload

Example Request:
POST http://localhost:8000/prices/poll
Request Body:
{
  "symbols": ["TSLA", "MSFT"],
  "provider": "yfinance",
  "interval": 20
}
Example Response:
{
  "job_id": "250cce99-b0de-4b4a-85f4-5fed2a132421",
  "status": "accepted",
  "config": {
    "symbols": ["TSLA", "MSFT"],
    "interval": 20,
    "provider": "yfinance"
  }
}




### Rate Limits
Planned: 60 req/min/IP

### Error Codes
- 400: Invalid request
- 404: Data not found
- 500: Internal error
